package com.heysig.companion

/** Release-specific data handling; no assertion about a recognition provider's retention. */
object PrivacyNotice {
    const val SYNTHESIS = "Voice prompts and spoken responses are separate optional settings. They use your installed text-to-speech engine, which may send reply text to its provider when a network voice is selected. Text status remains visible when speech is off."
    const val SPEECH = "Speech recognition uses your device's installed recognition service. It accesses your microphone and may send audio to its provider over the network under that provider's privacy policy. HeySig receives command text and alternatives, not a recording from that service. On the watch, those words are sent to the connected phone to interpret your request. Cancel sends no command. Use buttons or typed input instead if you do not want speech recognition. Optional spoken responses use a separate text-to-speech engine that may send reply text to its provider when a network voice is selected."
    val sections = listOf(
        "Privacy and data" to "HeySig uses your saved hearing-aid setup and requested settings to generate command tones. Playback completion does not confirm the aids received a change. Read the public policy for publisher contact details. If that link is unavailable, this candidate's public policy is not finalized.",
        "Saved on your devices" to "The phone stores fitting addresses, program names and capabilities, last-requested values, a saved restoration record, noise configuration and optional scalar calibration values with microphone/capture configuration, speech choices and disclosure choices in private app storage. The watch stores its selected phone, last request identifier and speech choices. These settings remain until you delete them or uninstall the app. Android app backup and device-to-device app-data extraction are disabled.",
        "Shake and vibration" to "Optional shake activation uses acceleration samples only in memory and stores a local On/Off choice separately on each device. A short vibration acknowledges activation. Phone shake requires listening On in an existing session; Off and Pause disable it. Watch shake can run in an explicitly started eight-hour microphone/motion foreground session, including while the screen sleeps. Each deliberate shake captures at most ten seconds through the installed recognition provider, after an optional prompt, and the microphone is idle between commands. The provider may send audio over its network. Phone speech switches control watch prompts and replies. A persistent notification offers Stop; Stop, Recents removal, expiry or process death ends the session, with no reboot restart. An explicitly started watch session can capture after a shake even while PIN-locked; it never unlocks or disables the PIN. Unlocking is required to start a new session. Motion can trigger recognition accidentally. No motion history is saved or uploaded.",
        "Hands-free microphone" to "Optional hands-free sessions use a bundled on-device keyword detector for Hey Sig, including while the phone is locked. Wake audio is processed in memory, not recorded or uploaded by the detector. Each following command uses up to ten seconds of recognition, preferring on-device recognition; an installed provider may send command audio over its network when on-device recognition is unavailable. No transcript history is added. Your selected watch may control listening and request commands during the session. Off releases the microphone but keeps session/watch control; End session stops both. Pause resumes after about 30 minutes, subject to Android timer delays. Sessions end after eight hours or process death and never restart after reboot. Background sounds or other people can trigger recognition; this is not speaker authentication. Hands-free disclosure/watch choices are stored locally; session mode and pause deadlines are memory-only. The offline engine/model notices are available on the phone in Privacy and data.",
        "Sleep routine" to "The phone stores saved bedtime/morning times, program slots, fitting/revision context, routine mode, manual override, schedule generations, due times, one-use playback claim identifiers and latest outcomes locally. Voice drafts stay in memory until Save and expire after five minutes. Separately reviewed automatic mode uses Android Alarms & reminders access and a short-lived visible playback service to send saved program commands while locked, without a tap. It uses the existing validated tone transport and records playback results, not hearing-aid receipt. Stop cancels future actions and requests cancellation; emitted tones cannot be undone. Manual changes pause automatic. Interrupted or more than two minutes late actions never replay. Reboot/update/clock changes only plan future events. Optional reminder mode posts notifications requiring your action and skips reminders over 15 minutes late. Neither mode starts a microphone, records audio, senses sleep or adds sleep tracking, sensor history or a network service. Routine data is included in optional local export and removed by Delete local app data.",
        "Noise microphone" to "Noise measurement uses the phone's microphone only after you request Sample, Observe, calibration or Automatic preview, review its explanation and grant permission. Bounded samples are processed in memory into relative sound statistics, then discarded. Calibration saves 18 relative level numbers and microphone/capture configuration locally when you save noise settings; unfinished calibration samples stay in memory. This feature does not save or upload recordings. Stop or leave HeySig to stop capture. Automatic noise switching remains disabled.",
        "Reviewed setup" to "Guided fitting drafts remain in memory for up to five minutes and require review before saving. Fitting imports read only addresses, program labels and tinnitus capabilities from a selected HeySig export; they never replay commands. Saving a changed fitting archives the previous fitting, requested values, restoration record and per-program targets locally (up to 20 archives), then clears active assumptions. Archives are included in optional local app-data export and removed by Delete local app data. Imported files and chosen document providers may contain or handle private settings.",
        "Personal phrases" to "Learning is optional. After a separate remember confirmation, the phone stores up to 200 exact phrase-to-command mappings, their setup context, source and confirmation time locally. Raw audio and conversation history are not required or saved by this feature. Learned phrases can apply to phone and watch input. Review, disable, forget or reset them in Voice and speech. Setup changes deactivate old mappings. Learning never sends or replays a hearing-aid command. Personal phrases are excluded from the general settings export. A separate optional export contains active phrase text and meanings; a chosen cloud document provider may upload it and exported copies must be deleted separately. Imports remain drafts until their mappings are reviewed and explicitly confirmed. Delete local app data removes local phrases.",
        "Optional speech" to SPEECH,
        "Spoken replies" to SYNTHESIS,
        "Watch Wi-Fi check" to "A requested watch Wi-Fi check passively observes Wi-Fi connection and Android internet-validation status for at most five seconds or until closed. It does not scan, collect network names/IP addresses, request location, save network history or change Wi-Fi. Check phone link separately sends a status request over the existing companion transport, which retains its normal bounded result history. Wi-Fi settings opens the watch’s system settings.",
        "Phone and watch messages" to "The phone/watch connection uses Wear OS Data Layer in Google Play services. Command text, recognition alternatives, request identifiers and replies (which can contain your requested hearing-aid settings) pass between your paired devices. Google manages encrypted transport; it may route data through Google-owned servers when Bluetooth is unavailable. The phone must stay open and unlocked with its watch connection enabled. Its explicit Enable choice is saved; returning to the unlocked phone app restores that foreground connection. Leaving or locking closes live authority immediately. Disconnect or Forget disables restoration. A saved watch selection alone does not enable it. Disconnect ends the session; interrupted requests are never automatically replayed.",
        "History and deletion" to "The phone keeps at most 64 watch result records for result lookup and replay protection. Records include identifiers, timestamps and reply text, which can contain settings. They expire after 24 hours and are removed on the next app open or history access. Speech alternatives and raw command text are not written to this history. Clear watch history to remove these records now. Clear display removes transient heard text. Delete local app data removes this device's saved setup and preferences without sending a command to the aids. Delete data separately on the other device. Provider-held speech or Google-service data must be managed with those providers.",
        "Export and third parties" to "Export is optional and writes your saved data to a location you choose with Android's document picker. That location may be a cloud provider; the exported file is outside HeySig's deletion controls. Protect exports because they can contain hearing-aid settings. Opening a public privacy link sends a normal browser request to the policy host. This app does not integrate advertising or analytics libraries; speech services, Google Play services, your operating system and chosen document providers have their own data practices that must be reviewed for the final release."
    )
}
